        <argsstring>)(void *lock_ctx)</argsstring>
        <name>lock</name>
        <qualifiedname>AVD3D12VADeviceContext::lock</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Callbacks for locking. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>They protect access to the internal staging texture (for <ref refid="hwcontext_8h_1abf1b1664b8239d953ae2cac8b643815a" kindref="member">av_hwframe_transfer_data()</ref> calls). They do NOT protect access to hwcontext or decoder state in general.</para>
<para>If unset on init, the hwcontext implementation will set them to use an internal mutex.</para>
<para>The underlying lock must be recursive. lock_ctx is for free use by the locking implementation. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
